WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.350
You've been acting weird recently.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.110
I was going to tell you once 
I got back, but whatever.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.100
What?

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.780
I'd like to dissolve our doubles team.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.300
Contacts

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.010
<b>Izumo Naohiro</b>

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.330
<b><i>Salaryman's Club</i></b>

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.000
<b><i>#09: Priority</i></b>

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.780
Tatsuru-san's on a business trip to Osaka.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:16.990
Why now?

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.390
Apparently the executive 
director's behind it.

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.590
Is it because of what happened 
at the izakaya the other day?

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:25.700
Revenge of the alien from Planet Green Onion.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.410
Wouldn't he go after Mikoto instead?

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.920
He couldn't get the job 
done if he'd been sent alone.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.730
See you guys later.

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.120
Uh, sure!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.120
Have a good night.

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.840
It's kind of scary how oddly calm he is.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.800
Yes, thank you.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.760
We'll deliver the goods tomorrow afternoon.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.570
Yes, we look forward to 
continuing to work with you.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.970
I was worried what would 
happen with Miyazumi gone,

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.020
but he's actually managing somehow.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.890
Shiratori's acting like an actual salesman.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.980
He's a little hard to approach, though.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.830
Yata-san, I sent you the sales slip. 
Could you check it for me?

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.030
Oh! Yes, sir!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.220
Huh? There's no delivery file for Waoko.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.680
Oh, that one? Miyazumi was 
looking at it last week.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.460
I'm always telling him to put things 
back when he's done using them.

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.770
Found it.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.300
<b>Medical Report</b>

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.300
<b></b>Name: Miyazumi Tatsuru-sama

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.300
<b></b>Medical ID Number: 88432

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.300
<b><b>Diagnosis: </b>Damaged anterior cruciate ligament</b>

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.300
<b></b>Notes: Currently receiving outpatient treatment for above condition. 
Recommended to avoid intense movement.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.250
What is this?

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.050
Sir, could you review this, please?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.010
Sure.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.790
Coach, look at this!

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:31.480
Focus on your job while you're at work!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.190
Tatsu's knee is at its limit.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:43.700
If he keeps up his current play style, his 
badminton career could end at any moment.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
<b>Medical Report</b>

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
<b></b>Name: Miyazumi Tatsuru-sama

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
<b></b>Medical ID Number: 88432

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
<b><b>Diagnosis: </b>Damaged anterior cruciate ligament</b>

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.700
<b></b>Notes: Currently receiving outpatient treatment for above condition. 
Recommended to avoid intense movement.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.450
Did he injure it during 
our recent Unisics match?

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.920
He's been dealing with 
this problem for a while,

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.870
and used every trick in the 
book to make it this far.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.780
He never said a word about this.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:58.460
He's not the kind of guy who complains.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.740
Especially not to you, his partner.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.920
Sorry, I overheard your conversation.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.880
Why does he have to be such a stranger?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.980
He could at least tell me. 
I'm a coach, after all.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.890
What would Izumo-san do?

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:20.780
Huh?

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.050
You know about him?

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.910
I met him at the corporate tournament.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:33.090
Who knows? He could be pretty unemotional.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.920
Why did he go to Mitsuhoshi, anyway?

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.400
We don't know exactly, either.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.640
Shortly after we were promoted out 
of the number two league last year,

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:46.900
Mitsuhoshi tried to poach Tatsu-san and 
Izumo, the key members of our team.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.390
Sounds like something Mitsuhoshi would do.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.880
Tatsu-san turned them down right away.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:55.140
Naturally, we assumed 
Izumo would say no, too.

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.830
But he left without a word.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:04.300
It's not that I don't understand 
how Tatsu-san feels.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:09.200
When you get to be around our age, you start 
wondering when's the right time to quit.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:10.700
He's being selfish.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.410
Huh?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.240
Hey, wait.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.780
<i>He's the one who dragged me into this.</i>

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:23.720
Yeah, I'm on my way home.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.240
<i>Everything you do is always so sudden.</i>

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.070
Hey, isn't that Ibuki?

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.300
It is!

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.670
He looks amazing in a kimono.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:35.100
I wonder if he'd give us his autograph.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.140
Doesn't exactly look approachable, though.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.960
<i>What's Ibuki-san doing here?</i>

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.220
Hey, Shiratori-kun.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:42.100
Huh?

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.660
I'm glad I ran into you.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.570
What?

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.820
Tokyo streets are so convoluted.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.290
Are you here for an interview 
today or something?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:55.850
Yeah. I thought I'd take care of some 
personal business while I was here,

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:57.620
but as you can see, I'm lost.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.790
Are you training by yourself today?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.840
I happened to be here to
 get my racket restrung.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.960
Ah... Oh, right. I saw your match 
against Unisics the other day.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.720
Huh?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.390
How does it feel to play doubles again?

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:13.840
I'm not in love with being pushed 
around by someone else.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:17.390
Miyazumi-san certainly is a powerful man.

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:20.100
He's selfish.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:25.930
Speaking of which, our Izumo said 
Miyazumi-san asked to see him.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.110
He said he'd go all the way 
to Kyoto to meet him.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:32.210
I guess they're still close. 
Not that I know anything about it.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:32.950
I...

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:39.160
I might go back to playing singles.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:42.130
I see.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:45.920
In that case, would you mind 
coming with me after this?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:48.380
Bicycles and 
Pedestrians Only

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:47.600
Huh?

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:51.760
Um, what are we doing here?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:55.420
This is the gym Mitsuhoshi uses
 while we're on the road.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.600
They know me here. Don't worry about it.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.860
That's not what I meant.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.440
As long as we're here, 
why don't we play a game?

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.570
Don't be so uptight.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.780
We can have a nice, casual game.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.290
<i>Drawn-out games against Ibuki-san 
put me at a disadvantage.</i>

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.760
Your side's wide open.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.220
19-6.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:38.180
Shiratori-kun, are you sure 
your instincts haven't dulled?

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.390
H-How is this a nice, casual game?

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:46.000
But a contest's a contest.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.980
If you lose, I don't want to hear 
you say that nonsense again.

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.990
<i>Wait, is he mad?</i>

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.410
<i>I'm not going down without a fight.</i>

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:07.840
One more point, and it's over.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.670
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:12.010
<i>My foresight's not working.</i>

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.930
<i>Is it because I'm playing against Ibuki-san?</i>

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.930
<i>Or because I haven't 
played singles in a while?</i>

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.890
<i>I don't know what happened,</i>

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:26.230
<i>but you think you can return 
to singles playing like that?</i>

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.190
<i>How naïve of you, Shiratori-kun.</i>

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.210
Looks like you finally noticed.

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:55.010
You're supposed to be playing singles, 
but you weren't playing like you were alone.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.290
Who does your heart fight alongside?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:16.610
I haven't had a SunBev craft beer in a while.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:17.650
Hey.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:20.530
Thanks for waiting.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.920
You had a lot of nerve back 
when you were a newbie.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.120
I'm five years older, and you refused 
to use honorifics when speaking to me.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.130
You were the one who told me I didn't have to.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.630
Most people would show 
a little more restraint.

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:40.390
Did you come here just to talk about this?

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:44.080
Out with it. There's no need for 
restraint between us now.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:52.190
Was it my fault you left SunBev?

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:57.880
You knew my knee was showing 
its age, didn't you?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:01.240
I couldn't help but notice it 
when playing with you.

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:09.290
I've always wondered if that's why you gave 
up on me and chose Mitsuhoshi instead.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.440
I honestly don't know if my 
continuing to play badminton

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:17.260
would be good for the team or him.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.720
Shiratori, right? He's still young.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:26.670
Playing doubles with Mikoto was 
supposed to be my last selfish act.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.940
But now I'm wondering if maybe 
I can actually keep playing.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.740
I want more.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:38.240
Give up.

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:42.950
You're right.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:46.240
Me putting an end to it is
 enough to satisfy you?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.140
Ridiculous.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:53.550
I chose Mitsuhoshi because there were 
only upsides to me joining their team.

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.460
Joining a strong team would get me 
closer to playing internationally.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:02.410
If you've got time to worry about it, 
go home and get some exercise.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:04.700
Izumo.

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:06.910
The next time we meet will 
be at the S/J League.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.230
What? You're not staying tonight?

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:15.710
I've got work tomorrow.

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:17.760
I just came to pick up some clothes.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:19.740
You'll stay for dinner, right?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:20.520
No, I—

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.400
I'll have dinner.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.280
Oh, by the way...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.680
Thanks for inviting me to 
the tasting the other day.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.790
When: <b>6/8 (Wed)</b>

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>We've developed 
new tasty products!</b>

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>Tasting Session</b>

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>Original Product</b>

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.790
<b>Sunlight Beverage</b>

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.790
It brought back memories.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:33.110
Brought back memories?

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:36.250
We lived around there for 
a little while a long time ago.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.120
What?

00:11:37.120 --> 00:11:41.890
You used to play all the time at
 that park with the hippo playground.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:43.560
Did I?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.100
<b>Micchan's Room</b>

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:49.680
I can't remember everything since 
I transferred schools so much.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:54.390
The hippo playground?

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.110
Did she mean <i>that</i> park?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:11:59.700
Excuse me...

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.530
Could I have some water?

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.540
What an awful first impression.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:13.880
How am I supposed to act 
when I see him tomorrow?

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:22.010
<b>General Purpose Notebook</b>

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.770
Hey, that's not food.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:25.930
Ugh, when is this from?

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:28.210
Wow, these suck.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.890
June 19th 
I went to the beach with my mom. 
There were lots of fish.
 I had fun. I want to go again.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:33.350
Huh?

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.440
Is this a shuttle feather?

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:46.130
<b>Me</b>

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:49.660
<b>My Friend</b>

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:47.080
"July 7th, sunny. Today was my last 
time playing badminton with my friend."

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:53.090
"When I grow up, I want 
to be a Badaryman, too."

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:58.260
Mikoto, dinner will be ready soon!

00:12:58.260 --> 00:12:59.100
Sorry!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:12.900
<i>Back then, I failed to achieve 
what I wanted to at SunBev.</i>

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.560
The badminton team lost in the first round.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.470
I heard the newbie who joined 
this year lost all his games.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:21.560
That Miyazumi guy?

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:23.900
He can't do his job, 
<i>and</i> he sucks at badminton.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.520
That's wage theft.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.750
Seriously.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:30.240
<i>You can't be serious.</i>

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.540
<i>I'm working practically full-time over here!</i>

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.670
<i>They don't know the first 
thing about badminton!</i>

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.210
<i>What's with him?</i>

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.040
What are you doing?

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:04.990
That was a nice hit.

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.200
Okay, again!

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:11.850
Nice shot.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:15.700
Hey!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.640
Mikoto!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.380
That was quite the fall.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.340
You don't need to try so 
hard to return everything.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.430
But I got it.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.290
You lose when it hits the ground, right?

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:42.410
I see. Yeah, you're right.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:43.830
That's exactly right.

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:49.240
<i>Those straightforward words opened my eyes.</i>

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:56.300
Take care even after you move, all right?

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.400
I don't wanna go.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:02.330
Here, you can have this.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:06.550
If you keep playing badminton, 
we'll meet again someday.

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:20.310
<i>Ten years later, when I found his name on 
the Mitsuhoshi roster, my mind was made up.</i>

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:26.730
But his record this past year has been awful.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Number 11</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Team</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Birthplace</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Date of Birth</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>May</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Height</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Weight</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Dominant Hand</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Right</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Singles</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>Player Quote</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>The Appeal of Badminton</b>

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.730
<b>...is clearly defined.</b>

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:31.620
I was bad at first, too, 
but you didn't give up on me.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.450
I'll make it work somehow.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:37.330
Please!

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:40.290
Fine.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:44.210
I'm betting on you. You and Shiratori.

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:46.840
Thank you!

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:59.020
<i>It was selfish of me to 
think I could save him.</i>

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.870
<i>But still, I...</i>

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:04.490
There you are!

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.400
What are you doing here?

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.490
I'll make it work somehow.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:18.470
Your knee, I mean. And your play style...

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:20.470
We can talk about it, and make some changes.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:24.540
I don't have any concrete 
ideas right now, but...

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:26.960
No, wait. That's not what I wanted to say.

00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:28.430
Ah, screw it.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.720
Please play with me again!

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.700
You're the one who taught me.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:49.110
I'll be a Badaryman until the day I die.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:58.410
<b>Saitama Matsugishi Public Elementary</b>

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.740
Too slow!

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:01.950
Don't go slacking off on me!

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:02.950
Yes, sir!

00:17:03.260 --> 00:17:05.390
Come on! Return, return, return!

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:10.250
You'd better practice with me today.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.910
Sorry, can't today, either.

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:12.630
What?

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:15.090
Where are you going every week—

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:17.140
Wait, do you actually have a girlfriend?

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.970
You wanna come with me?

00:17:20.590 --> 00:17:21.370
Huh?

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.820
Come on, your feet have stopped moving again.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.130
Nakamori-sensei, go easy on me.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.900
That wouldn't be good for you.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:35.360
Huh?

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:41.610
Coach Nakamori is Coach Ono's junior.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:46.170
He introduced me to him when I was 
struggling with how to use my body better.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:50.590
In the world of para-athletes, 
power alone isn't enough to win.

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:55.470
My personal theory is that a flexible body 
and the mental strength necessary

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.590
to maintain your pace no matter 
what are what's important.

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.380
"Definitely a girlfriend," my ass.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.210
Huh?

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.390
Nothing.

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:09.350
How could you tell me to rely on my 
teammate and not mention this to me?

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:12.030
What? Are you mad at me?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:19.700
Okay, now that Shiratori-kun's here, 
let's come up with a new play style.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.820
Yes, sir.

